{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793600488350890610,"compiled_state":{"alias":"peerless-treelike-adouri","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":1},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3898455d4f542399b2507cdd79bf6a2618c59162f2e31107c1f33c61ee2ff942","event_uuid":"f4e86dbb-5d62-4a3b-a542-ad7cb9fc1985","position":{"commit_sha":"575af86a628da67842b5451390fa80f938a70897","position":"1793594063428503848-f4e86dbb-5d62-4a3b-a542-ad7cb9fc1985"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c52b3408898925cd399774a4e9c32a85311e33be98827b0af8dd2d93fbb65bc2","event_uuid":"72ade0f7-d083-4e69-89ef-c13046d03f50","position":{"commit_sha":"cb6a8711cb998901e3b981925324fe51c5494604","position":"1793594079210234701-72ade0f7-d083-4e69-89ef-c13046d03f50"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"bf255155f483fb22b808eac861592b74cf20f24902e6ac0e82f5572dacf18171","event_uuid":"ffabf1f6-268d-4302-9d47-0871fc82f457","position":{"commit_sha":"2d8af3317b4c37f59a36b37fc2bcae7417c47deb","position":"1793594088334100800-ffabf1f6-268d-4302-9d47-0871fc82f457"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"39324d1e4d659b2651dabd6eb1e990baa840ceb7b2705db7bdb56b55f9d7fcc0","event_uuid":"bc4b79ed-300c-4aa1-92f7-c39f47ab7052","position":{"commit_sha":"7646b58ad9119971b23868f14f3975663f33c134","position":"1793594095478077457-bc4b79ed-300c-4aa1-92f7-c39f47ab7052"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793594063428503848,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"72ade0f7-d083-4e69-89ef-c13046d03f50","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88"}],"description":"## What is wrong\n\n`src/rebar/similar/catchup.py` keys the `docs` row inconsistently between the two paths that write it.\n\n`_reindex` treats the directory name and the reduced ticket id as potentially different values. It deletes under **both** keys before inserting:\n\n```python\nkeys = {dir_name} | ({doc[0]} if doc else set())\nconn.executemany(\"DELETE FROM docs WHERE ticket_id = ?\", [(k,) for k in keys])\n```\n\nand then inserts under `doc[0]`, which `_document` computes as `str(state.get(\"ticket_id\") or dir_name)`.\n\nThe removal path in `_apply` deletes under **only** the directory name:\n\n```python\nfor dir_name in removed:\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM docs WHERE ticket_id = ?\", (dir_name,))\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM dirstate WHERE dir_name = ?\", (dir_name,))\n```\n\nSo when a reduced `ticket_id` differs from its directory name, the row was inserted under the ticket id, the delete matches nothing, and the `docs` row outlives the directory. The `dirstate` row is removed correctly, so catch-up never revisits that directory and the orphan is never reclaimed. It stays searchable, meaning `find_similar` can return a ticket that no longer exists.\n\nThe defect is the inconsistency itself: the code defends against divergence in `_reindex` and not in `_apply`.\n\n## Reachability — latent, not live\n\nMeasured against the live store at `.tickets-tracker`: all 9874 active ticket directories reduce to a `ticket_id` equal to their directory name, so 0 directories can currently produce the orphan. The defect cannot be triggered in this store today, which is why it was filed rather than fixed inside `47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88`.\n\nThat measurement is a statement about present data, not an invariant. Nothing in the schema or the store-walk enforces `ticket_id == dir_name`, and `_document`'s `or dir_name` fallback plus `_reindex`'s dual-key delete both exist precisely because the code does not assume it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test builds an index over a ticket directory whose reduced `ticket_id` differs from its directory name, removes the directory, runs catch-up, and asserts no `docs` row survives for that ticket.\n- [ ] A test asserts `find_similar` does not return a removed ticket under that same divergent-name condition.\n- [ ] The removal path and the reindex path agree on the key, so a single documented key governs both. Either the removal path deletes under the same key set `_reindex` uses, or `docs` carries the directory name and both paths key on it.\n- [ ] The chosen key is stated in `catchup.py`'s module docstring, so the next reader does not have to infer it from two call sites.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Provenance\n\nRaised as an advisory (non-blocking) correctness finding by the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on change 3211 patchset 2, against `src/rebar/similar/catchup.py:198-200`. Verified by reading both call sites and by measuring divergence across the live store.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/similar/catchup.py","reason":"align the removal path docs key with the reindex path key; state the governing key in the module docstring"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_similar_tickets_index.py","reason":"divergent dir_name/ticket_id removal tests: no surviving docs row, and find_similar does not return the removed ticket"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","similar-tickets"],"ticket_id":"adc7-2aba-2995-439a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Similar-index removal deletes the docs row by dir_name while reindex keys it by reduced ticket_id","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f4e86dbb-5d62-4a3b-a542-ad7cb9fc1985","72ade0f7-d083-4e69-89ef-c13046d03f50","ffabf1f6-268d-4302-9d47-0871fc82f457","bc4b79ed-300c-4aa1-92f7-c39f47ab7052","fe8da20d-2a22-42c5-9b2f-2e5b2b0a07ff"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793600488350890610,"uuid":"d3036b66-dfdd-47e6-a296-95becb3a73c6"}